WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.467
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Idioms from Shakespeare

00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:03.594
1

00:00:03.827 --> 00:00:05.314
Noun phrases

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.350
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1, B

00:00:09.277 --> 00:00:13.032
<v><b>M:</b></v> ‘the be-all and end-all’ means the most important thing

00:00:14.918 --> 00:00:17.157
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2, F

00:00:18.978 --> 00:00:23.194
<v><b>M:</b></v> ‘in one fell swoop’ means all at once, in one go

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.645
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3, D

00:00:28.559 --> 00:00:32.004
<v><b>M:</b></v> ‘a sorry sight’ means in a bad state, a mess

00:00:33.778 --> 00:00:36.236
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4, A

00:00:37.089 --> 00:00:39.879
<v><b>F:</b></v> ‘elbow room’ means space to move

00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:44.125
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5, C

00:00:44.998 --> 00:00:48.766
<v><b>M:</b></v> ‘a wild goose chase’ means a useless search for something

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:53.229
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6, E

00:00:54.081 --> 00:00:57.332
<v><b>F:</b></v> ‘Good riddance!’ means I’m so glad they’ve gone

00:00:59.272 --> 00:01:01.758
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 7, G

00:01:02.691 --> 00:01:05.127
<v><b>M:</b></v> ‘his own flesh and blood’ means family